    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -680,
        "y": -300
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Ioffe and Szegedy, \"Batch Normalization: Accelerating Deep Network Training by Reducing Internal Covariate Shift\", ICML 2015. Claim: normalising each layer's inputs over the mini-batch lets a network train at a much higher learning rate and converge in fewer steps. Recipe: two 784-256-256-256-10 ReLU MLPs on 10,000 MNIST images, plain SGD at lr 0.5 for 3 epochs, one with BatchNorm1d after each hidden Linear. Under seed 0 on a CPU the BatchNorm net's training loss falls from 0.43 to 0.11 and it scores 0.90 on the test set. The plain net at the same rate is still at 2.11 after 3 epochs and scores 0.18, close to chance (0.10).\n\nIoffe 與 Szegedy，〈Batch Normalization: Accelerating Deep Network Training by Reducing Internal Covariate Shift〉，ICML 2015。論點：在每個 mini-batch 上把每一層的輸入正規化，網路就能用高得多的學習率訓練，而且更少步就收斂。配方：兩個 784-256-256-256-10 的 ReLU MLP，在 10,000 張 MNIST 影像上用 lr 0.5 的純 SGD 訓練 3 個 epoch，其中一個在每個隱藏層的 Linear 後面加 BatchNorm1d。在 CPU 上以種子 0 執行，BatchNorm 網路的訓練損失從 0.43 降到 0.11，測試準確率 0.90。同樣學習率下，一般網路 3 個 epoch 後損失仍是 2.11，測試準確率 0.18，接近亂猜（0.10）。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "start",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -420,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 360
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-data",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 1000,
        "y": -300
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "MNIST ships with the repository under backend/data, so the run reads it from disk. DatasetSplit keeps a fixed 10,000 of the 60,000 training images; its own seed (0) picks them, so every arm trains on the same images through the one DataLoader.\n\nMNIST 隨專案放在 backend/data 底下，執行時直接從磁碟讀取。DatasetSplit 從 60,000 張訓練影像中固定留下 10,000 張，挑哪幾張由它自己的種子（0）決定，所以每一組都透過同一個 DataLoader 在同一批影像上訓練。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "dl-train",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 320,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-arms",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -300,
        "y": 400
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Each arm has its own SequentialModel node. One model node wired into two TrainingLoops would hand every loop the same weights, and each loop would continue from what the previous one left. The run seed (0, stored in the file) fixes the shuffle order, any dropout masks and each model's initial weights. Every node is seeded from the run seed and its own id, so the arms start from different draws of the same initialisation. With Persist weights between runs on (Settings > Training Behavior), a second Run continues from the trained weights; turn it off to repeat these numbers.\n\n每一組都有自己的 SequentialModel 節點。如果一個模型節點同時接到兩個 TrainingLoop，每個迴圈拿到的是同一份權重，後跑的會接著前一個留下的結果繼續訓練。執行種子（0，存在檔案裡）固定了洗牌順序、dropout 遮罩和每個模型的初始權重。每個節點的種子由執行種子和節點自己的 id 推得，所以各組的初始權重是同一種初始化方式下的不同抽樣。在設定 > 訓練行為中開啟「在多次執行間保留權重」時，第二次執行會從訓練過的權重繼續；關閉它才能重現這些數字。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "model-plain",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -340,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-model",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -300,
        "y": 1400
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Open the layer editor: Flatten -> three blocks of Linear -> BatchNorm1d -> ReLU (256 units each) -> Linear 256->10. The model above is the same without the BatchNorm1d layers. In eval mode, which EvaluateModel uses, BatchNorm normalises with the running mean and variance it collected during training.\n\n打開圖層編輯器：Flatten -> 三個 Linear -> BatchNorm1d -> ReLU 區塊（各 256 個單元）-> Linear 256->10。上面那個模型相同，只是沒有 BatchNorm1d。EvaluateModel 使用 eval 模式，此時 BatchNorm 用訓練期間累積的平均值與變異數來正規化。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "model-bn",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -340,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-lr",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 360,
        "y": 740
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "lr 0.5 is far above what this plain MLP trains well with. Its updates overshoot and the loss stays near 2.30, the loss of a uniform guess over 10 digits. Set this optimizer to lr 0.05 and rerun to watch the plain net learn at a rate it tolerates.\n\nlr 0.5 遠高於這個一般 MLP 能好好訓練的範圍。它的更新會衝過頭，損失停在 2.30 附近，也就是對 10 個數字平均亂猜的損失。把這個 Optimizer 改成 lr 0.05 再執行一次，就能看到一般網路在它承受得了的學習率下學起來。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "opt-plain",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 340
        },
        "noteWidth": 300
      }
    }
  ],
